  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>&#8203;</mtext> <mrow> <mtext>28</mtext></mrow> </msub> <mtext>Ni</mtext></mrow> </math> has <math> <mrow> <mtext>+2</mtext></mrow> </math> oxidation state and since the complex is Diamagnetic, all electrons are paired in inner 3d, orbital to provide the electronic configuration as under:<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fdee779b-8b90-4beb-b1ac-66d6a8316378-image.png\" style=\"width: 450px; height: 143px;\" /><br /><math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>L</mtext> <mo>&#8722;</mo> </msup> </mrow> </math> might have been a strong field like <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mtext>CN</mtext></mrow> <mo>&#8722;</mo> </msup> <mo>.</mo></mrow> </math> Hybridisation is <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mtext>dsp</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msup> <mtext>.</mtext></mrow> </math> Number of unpaired electrons = <math> <mtext>0</mtext> </math></p></blockquote>",
